---
title: "Introduction to Problem Solving and Programming"
code: "CSC-221"
category: "computer-science"
credits: "3"
prerequisites: []
corequisites: []
---

Introduces problem solving and implementation of solutions using a high-level programming language in a structured programming environment. Includes concepts and practice of structured programming, problem-solving, top-down design of algorithms, a high-level programming language syntax, control structures, arrays, and an introduction into object-oriented programming. First course in a three-course sequence (CSC 221, CSC 222, CSC 223). The assignments in this course require mathematical problem-solving skills, algebraic modeling and functions, and use of variables. Lecture 3 hours. Total 3 hours per week. Additional course fee applies.
